# controller-manager hidraw gate (see controller-hidraw-gate).
#
# While a pad is gated (marker under /run/controller-manager/gated), its
# hidraw nodes must be BORN inaccessible: the gate rebinds the HID driver to
# revoke existing fds, and without this rule the reborn node would be open
# for a moment - long enough for Steam's udev hotplug to reopen it.
#
# Filename 72-: AFTER the whole 71-*-controllers.rules family - steam-devices
# ships e.g. 71-sony-controllers.rules, which re-adds MODE 0660 and the
# uaccess tag for DualSense hidraw and must not get the last word (verified
# in the field: with this rule at 71-, the pad's node came back 0660+ACL and
# Steam repainted the lightbar in a gated mode). Still BEFORE
# 73-seat-late.rules, which turns the uaccess tag into a seat-user ACL that
# would tunnel through MODE 0000 - removing the tag here prevents that, and
# TAG-= has no final-assignment form, so the ordering is what protects it.
# MODE/GROUP use ':=' (final assignment): no later rule can override them.
#
# KERNELS matches the parent HID device name (BUS:VVVV:PPPP.NNNN) so the
# helper only ever runs for Sony/Microsoft pads, not for every HID device.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="????:054C:*|????:045E:*", \
  PROGRAM=="/usr/local/bin/controller-hidraw-gate udev-check %p", \
  MODE:="0000", GROUP:="root", TAG-="uaccess"
